{"text": "aT. S. OSDENE\nJANS 1986\n\nNational Academy of Sciences Presentation\n\nETS and Cardiorespiratory Disorders\n\nPhilip Witorsch\nDivision of Pulmonary Diseases and Allergy\nDepartment of Medicine\nThe George Washington University Medical Center\nThis presentation focuses on the possible effects\nof Environmental Tobacco Smoke (\"ETS\") on the cardiovascular\nand respiratory systems in adults and children. Before\nexamining the individual studies that have attempted to\naddress this area, some preliminary observations may be in\norder.\nSeveral criteria must be satisfied, of course,\nbefore a study can be said to support a causal hypothesis\nthat would link environmental exposure -- whether to ETS or\nany other substance or agent -- and adverse health effects.\nThe following criteria apply to both epidemiological and\n\nclinical experimental studie\n\n1, Estimates or measurements of exposure and/or\ndose must be accurate and verifiable. This means, among\nother things, that any questionnaires or instruments that are\nused must be appropriate to the situation, standardized,\nvalidated and used in a scientifically acceptable manner.\n2. The study must be rigorously and appropriately\n\ndesigned. This requires adequate sample size, the use of\n\n6EST9I80S02\n\nappropriate study and control groups, including acceptable", "words": [{"text": "aT.", "x0": 122, "y0": 24, "x1": 142, "y1": 39, "conf": 48.0}, {"text": "S.", "x0": 149, "y0": 22, "x1": 159, "y1": 38, "conf": 78.0}, {"text": "OSDENE", "x0": 170, "y0": 21, "x1": 243, "y1": 37, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "JANS", "x0": 142, "y0": 61, "x1": 181, "y1": 77, "conf": 81.0}, {"text": "1986", "x0": 201, "y0": 62, "x1": 228, "y1": 77, "conf": 46.0}, {"text": "National", "x0": 175, "y0": 117, "x1": 247, "y1": 128, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Academy", "x0": 257, "y0": 117, "x1": 320, "y1": 130, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "of", "x0": 331, "y0": 116, "x1": 348, "y1": 126, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Sciences", "x0": 359, "y0": 11